" The editors demo's overlay vimrc (docs/tapes/fixtures.sh, up:editors): the
" minimum that earns hi's `vim -u`, vim's own shipped defaults.

" must be first: `vim -u <file>` implies 'compatible', which disables <> key
" notation and a good deal else. defaults.vim clears it too, but that file is
" not on every vim.
set nocompatible

" the out-of-the-box editor rather than the 1976 one, spelled the way vim
" itself spells it. `unlet!` because a system vimrc may have set the skip flag;
" `silent!` because a vim old enough not to ship the file would error on it.
unlet! skip_defaults_vim
silent! source $VIMRUNTIME/defaults.vim

" belt and braces for a vim old enough to have no defaults.vim; where that file
" did load it set both already, and setting them twice costs nothing.
syntax enable
filetype plugin indent on
